1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,688
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:32,866
[Emilia] <i>Today marks the death</i>
<i>of Miss Ivy Aguas!</i>

6
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:34,617
[Ivy] <i>What are you going to do?!</i>

7
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,910
-<i>Let me go!</i>
-[Julio] <i>Goodbye, Miss Aguas!</i>

8
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:37,662
<i>Let go! What are you doing?!</i>

9
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:40,874
[Julio] <i>You have outdone</i>
<i>yourself this time.</i>

10
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:43,877
<i>You have proven yourself</i>
<i>beyond all my imagination.</i>

11
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:47,213
<i>Truly you have Ardiente blood</i>
<i>running in your veins.</i>

12
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:48,798
[Ivy] <i>Help!</i>

13
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,301
<i>-Five, six, seven, eight…</i>
<i>-Help!</i>

14
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:53,553
<i>I'm down here! Somebody help me!</i>

15
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:55,930
[Natalie] <i>Choose where your loyalties lie.</i>

16
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:58,266
<i>With your friends? Or with me?</i>

17
00:00:58,349 --> 00:00:59,934
<i>Them or me?</i>

18
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:03,271
-[Diego] <i>Dad, where is Ivy?</i>
-[Raul] <i>Ivy Aguas is in danger.</i>

19
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:06,024
<i>The Ardientes buried her alive.</i>
<i>You have to find and save her.</i>

20
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,984
<i>She only has a few hours left.</i>

21
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:08,985
-[screaming]
-[glass breaks]

22
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:12,238
<i>They buried her alive</i>
<i>just like what they did to me before!</i>

23
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:14,783
[Damian] <i>Now that I'm here, I'll help you.</i>

24
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:19,871
[Ivy] <i>I won't lose hope.</i>
<i>I believe in miracles.</i>

25
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:22,373
<i>What I want from you is the assurance</i>

26
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:25,960
<i>that Ivy Aguas is in that plywood box,</i>

27
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,921
<i>dead or alive.</i>

28
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:31,007
<i>If we have to dig up every grave,</i>
<i>so be it.</i>

29
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:34,344
<i>As long as we find her.</i>
<i>We have to find her, understood?</i>

30
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:36,846
[Arthur] <i>Wait! What if they gun us down?!</i>

31
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,264
[Diego] <i>We need to move!</i>

32
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,933
<i>We don't have time.</i>

33
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,267
<i>Ivy, we're here.</i>

34
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:43,353
<i>Don't worry, we'll save you.</i>

35
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:44,604
<i>Just hold on.</i>

36
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:48,858
[Diego] There are guards everywhere,
but we can do this.

37
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,446
Thank you, Diego.

38
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,949
Don't worry, Ivy. We'll save you.

39
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:57,325
<i>Hang in there.</i>

40
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:01,329
I won't--

41
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:04,791
I won't let go.

42
00:02:09,712 --> 00:02:10,880
[phone chimes]

43
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:15,426
[tense music playing]

44
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,642
[moans]

45
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:28,314
[labored breathing]

46
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:35,572
[foreboding music playing]

47
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:40,493
[man] Where are we headed to, boss?

48
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,996
How much will we get for this?

49
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:44,706
Just do as I say.

50
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,838
We just want to make sure

51
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:53,923
that our efforts
won't be for nothing, boss.

52
00:02:54,507 --> 00:02:57,302
This mission is more important than money.

53
00:02:58,428 --> 00:02:59,512
Madrigal.

54
00:03:00,889 --> 00:03:02,307
Are we clear about this?

55
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:06,394
Your targets are Jaguar and the Ardientes.

56
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:11,232
-I haven't forgotten our deal.
-I'm just making sure.

57
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:14,068
So, what's the plan with Julio?

58
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:16,988
Are we going to send Emilia back to jail?

59
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:18,907
No.

60
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:20,366
Then what?

61
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:30,043
Ma'am, I know I am indebted
to you for saving my life.

62
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:34,172
But if you won't take advantage
of this opportunity…

63
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:37,508
let's just forget about our deal.

64
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:41,679
[tense music playing]

65
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:53,566
May we leave now?

66
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:55,652
Yes.

67
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:58,696
Let's go.

68
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:05,161
-[car engine starts]
-Follow them.

69
00:04:19,175 --> 00:04:22,136
[foreboding music playing]

70
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:24,055
[Jose] Everything's set

71
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:26,516
for the centennial celebration, Governor.

72
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:28,518
Very good.

73
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:34,274
But I still want you to deploy
more bodyguards for me

74
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:36,901
as well as for Emilia.

75
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:40,530
We have to keep our guards up,

76
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:43,366
especially against Diego Torillo's ploys.

77
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,576
You know, I wonder…

78
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:49,497
Where does that bastard
get the guts he has now?

79
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:52,250
Maybe because Ivy Aguas
is on his side, sir.

80
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:53,459
[scoffs]

81
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:58,381
I already have Ivy Aguas.

82
00:04:59,048 --> 00:05:02,510
I expect him to crumble and beg…

83
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:05,013
instead of going head to head with me

84
00:05:05,096 --> 00:05:06,431
just to unseat me.

85
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:12,854
Not unless

86
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:16,941
he's got himself a new ally.

87
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:22,030
Colonel, I want you to find out

88
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:26,492
if there are other supporters of
Diego's complaint against me.

89
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:29,746
-[Jose] Yes, Governor.
-Go.

90
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:41,883
-Raul, where are you going?
-Papa.

91
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:46,512
Huh? Uh… I just have to…
meet a client of mine.

92
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,723
-Client?
-Yes.

93
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:50,850
All right.

94
00:05:51,684 --> 00:05:55,021
[tense music playing]

95
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:00,359
[door closes]

96
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:13,122
-Come on! We need to act now!
-Just wait!

97
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:17,210
[Arthur] Who's that?

98
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:19,837
Hello, Dad?

99
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,257
Diego… Where are you, son?

100
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,258
I'll help you.

101
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:27,637
There's too many of them, Dad.
It's too dangerous.

102
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,640
Son, I helped you before,
and I will continue to do so.

103
00:06:30,723 --> 00:06:33,392
<i>Right now, we're the only ones</i>
<i>who have each other's backs.</i>

104
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:35,186
So we need to work together.

105
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:38,064
I'm begging you, son. Let's work together.

106
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:50,409
Auntie…

107
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,329
There's still no update…

108
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,207
from Diego and Jepoy.

109
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:00,503
I'm sure they're just busy, Anna.

110
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:04,590
Yes, Auntie.

111
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,009
You're right.

112
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:12,932
Both Diego and Jepoy won't stop
until they save Lily.

113
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:16,853
They'll bring Lily home.

114
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,898
They'll find my daughter.

115
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:25,945
They'll dig her out of the grave
she's buried in.

116
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:31,033
Anna, Lily's been through so much.

117
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:34,745
This won't take her down.

118
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:37,415
[Camia weeps]

119
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,709
My daughter will live.

120
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:44,422
She, not the Ardientes, will live on.

121
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:47,884
She won't die at the hands
of the Ardientes.

122
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,474
Not to them.

123
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:56,267
[Camia sobbing]

124
00:07:57,768 --> 00:08:00,813
[whimpering]

125
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:05,943
[weeping] Lily…

126
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:07,904
[sobs]

127
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:12,116
[breathing heavily]

128
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:19,749
[pensive music playing]

129
00:08:21,375 --> 00:08:22,543
[pants]

130
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:27,965
[phone ringing]

131
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,469
[Emilia] <i>Hello, Ivy!</i>

132
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:33,638
I thought you were dead already.

133
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,640
Why, Emilia…

134
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,768
Did you miss me?

135
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,019
[chuckles]

136
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,939
Oh, it must be the other way around.

137
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:44,690
<i>You're the one who misses me.</i>

138
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:47,652
<i>Because life down there must be so boring</i>

139
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:50,446
with no company except darkness.

140
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:54,408
It gets so lonely, right?

141
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,452
Inside that box, I mean.

142
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,412
[chuckles]

143
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:03,084
[weakly] You know, Emilia,
you don't have to imagine it.

144
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,670
<i>If you want,</i>

145
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:08,464
we could trade places.

146
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:11,259
-Come on.
-[laughs] That's so funny.

147
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:13,135
And that will never happen, okay?

148
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:15,555
But, hey, let me tell you something, Ivy.

149
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,933
<i>You know, according to research</i>

150
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:22,478
a person buried alive

151
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:25,523
has only, like,
five and a half hours to live.

152
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,067
<i>Then, after that…</i>

153
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,110
hmm…

154
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:34,991
There can be suffocation,
disorientation, and dizziness.

155
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:37,743
If that happens, after all that,

156
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:38,744
you're going to die.

157
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:41,706
<i>Oh! Poor Ivy.</i>

158
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:45,251
And according to
my calculations right now,

159
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:49,088
you only got like an hour to go, and then…

160
00:09:49,171 --> 00:09:50,840
-<i>Bye-bye, cruel world!</i>
-[thumps]

161
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,968
Oh! That must be so exciting
for you, Ivy, huh?

162
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:55,469
[thumps]

163
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:57,096
<i>I know what you're doing.</i>

164
00:09:57,179 --> 00:09:58,764
You're trying to save your breath.

165
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:00,308
But time is running out.

166
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:02,560
-<i>And here it goes…</i>
-[moans]

167
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:05,313
Time starts now.

168
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:06,939
Tick-tock!

169
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,566
<i>Tick-tock!</i>

170
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,235
[laughing]

171
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,696
-[Emilia continues laughing]
-[pants]

172
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,364
[laughing]

173
00:10:16,365 --> 00:10:17,450
[Ivy] <i>Emilia…</i>

174
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:21,579
[weakly] I'll repeat myself.

175
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:29,920
[emphatic] I'm Ivy Aguas.

176
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:37,970
I can handle everything.

177
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:41,349
-<i>Remember?</i>
-Okay. If you think that way.

178
00:10:41,432 --> 00:10:42,475
<i>But you know?</i>

179
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:44,101
<i>If you're going to be nice to me, Ivy,</i>

180
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,519
who knows?

181
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:47,480
I might change my mind.

182
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:51,609
[weakly] Oh, Emilia.

183
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:58,324
You just never get tired
of talking, do you?

184
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:01,535
Is that all you want to say?

185
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:06,540
Because I don't want you

186
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:11,003
to be the last person I talk to if,

187
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:14,215
<i>and only if,</i>

188
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:16,467
I die today.

189
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:18,052
[Emilia] <i>Hey!</i>

190
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,428
You listen to me…

191
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:21,806
I know exactly what you're trying to do.

192
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:26,185
<i>You're trying to save</i>
<i>your breath and your battery.</i>

193
00:11:26,268 --> 00:11:28,979
But I'm going to do the exact opposite.

194
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:31,148
I'm going to drain the air
out of your lungs

195
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:34,193
along with your phone battery
until you die!

196
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:37,571
<i>And what makes you think that</i>
<i>you can get out of that grave?</i>

197
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:40,491
No! You will be stuck there!

198
00:11:40,574 --> 00:11:42,201
[laughs]

199
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,331
[sighs deeply]

200
00:11:47,415 --> 00:11:48,999
[Diego] Batch, what now?

201
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,793
There's a dozen of them in there.

202
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:52,670
They all have guns.
We are no match for them!

203
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:53,963
I don't care!

204
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:56,173
We're going to save Ivy
no matter what happens.

205
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,467
All right. We're going to cripple them.

206
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:01,303
We're going to take them out
one by one. Let's go.

207
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:04,598
Batch, wait. Let's fall back.
There are too many of them!

208
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:07,393
If you want to go home, then go home.

209
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:08,894
I'm going to save Ivy.

210
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:10,271
-Wait.
-Diego!

211
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:15,818
[panting]

212
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,779
[goon 1] Just stay here for a bit.

213
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:20,281
-Okay.
-We'll stay here.

214
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:23,033
Keep your eyes peeled.
Don't let anyone get past you.

215
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,167
-[thwacks]
-[groans]

216
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:34,628
[suspenseful music playing]

217
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:39,383
[goon grunting]

218
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:41,552
Diego!

219
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:47,266
[goons grunting]

220
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:49,727
[goon 1] Sir! Sir!

221
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,228
-[goon 2] The other one!
-[goon 1] Yes, sir!

222
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:52,646
[goon 3] We have company!

223
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:56,650
You want to be heroes, huh?

224
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:02,198
[suspenseful music playing]

225
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:06,827
[clatters]

226
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:24,970
[tense music playing]

227
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:29,808
Our targets are Julio Ardiente's men.

228
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,393
You, go there! You two, there!

229
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,603
-Where?
-[thwacks]

230
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:42,738
[tense music playing]

231
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:45,783
[goon] This is the end for you!

232
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,202
-[Jepoy] Get down!
-[gunshots]

233
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:51,497
Diego!

234
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:53,582
[gunfire]

235
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:55,834
[goon] Retreat!

236
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,545
[gunfire continues]

237
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:00,381
Let's go! Come on! Come on!

238
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,591
[gunshot]

239
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:09,223
[tense music playing]

240
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:10,516
[Raul] What are you doing here?

241
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:13,602
Don't tell me you want
to join the party too.

242
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:16,272
[Damian] That's where you're wrong.

243
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:21,068
I'm here to help Ivy Aguas.

244
00:14:24,029 --> 00:14:26,073
[gunfire]

245
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:39,461
[gunfire continues]

246
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,546
Jepoy!

247
00:14:42,673 --> 00:14:47,011
[gunfire continues]

248
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,391
[Marlon] Hide, Batch!

249
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:53,767
-Cover! Cover!
-Diego! Diego!

250
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:55,978
[gunfire continues]

251
00:14:58,105 --> 00:15:02,109
[suspenseful music playing]

252
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:06,530
[gunfire continues]

253
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:09,033
[Raul] Don't tell me you've
suddenly grown a conscience?

254
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:11,452
Do you really expect me to believe that?

255
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:16,290
You'll have to go through me
before you can do your plans.

256
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:22,338
I'm going to kill you first
before you can stop me!

257
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:29,762
[suspenseful music playing]

258
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:43,776
[both grunting]

259
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:50,282
You bastard! You can never
change who you are!

260
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:53,535
You can't! You are evil to the core!

261
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:56,205
Even the devil himself
would look up to you!

262
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:57,539
You're one to talk!

263
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:00,876
What's your reason for helping Ivy Aguas?!

264
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,212
Don't tell me you've grown
a conscience too!

265
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:07,132
A criminal will never trust
another criminal.

266
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:12,346
I will only trust you if you
show me your true identity.

267
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:13,555
[groans]

268
00:16:14,014 --> 00:16:18,602
[both grunting]

269
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:35,411
[tense music playing]

270
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:39,832
[gunshot]

271
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:47,548
[tense music playing]

272
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:50,467
Diego?

273
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:51,802
[gunshots]

274
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,846
[ominous music playing]

275
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:57,266
[thumping]

276
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,309
Diego…

277
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:00,936
[pants] Die--

278
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,689
Diego, I'm here… [pants]

279
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:05,274
Jepoy! That's where Ivy is!

280
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:08,318
[gunfire]

281
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:11,447
-Are you sure she's there?
-Yes!

282
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:13,699
If Ivy isn't there,
we'll be wasting precious time!

283
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:15,576
I'm sure that's where they buried her!

284
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:16,785
-[gunshot]
-[Jepoy groans]

285
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:20,998
[gunfire continues]

286
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:26,670
[tense music playing]

287
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,922
[gun clatters]

288
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:34,553
[suspenseful music playing]

289
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:40,434
[laughs mockingly]

290
00:17:41,226 --> 00:17:43,145
What, you actually thought you shot me?

291
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:44,730
Tough luck.

292
00:17:45,397 --> 00:17:47,566
I told you we'd fight to the death, right?

293
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:51,361
[groans]

294
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:56,742
[gunfire continues]

295
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:58,994
[thumping]

296
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:01,705
You know what, Ivy?

297
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:04,500
<i>Let me check again with you later, huh?</i>

298
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,667
<i>And don't you worry…</i>

299
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:09,046
I'm going to give you your
moment to shine before you die.

300
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:10,589
Bye!

301
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:13,050
[exhales]

302
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:16,095
[gunfire in distance]

303
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:17,679
Diego!

304
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:20,474
Ivy's running out of time.
We need to hurry.

305
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:22,184
Hang in there, Ivy!

306
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,686
[thumping]

307
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:26,730
Diego…

308
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,148
Diego, I'm here!

309
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:32,069
[gunfire in distance]

310
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:35,072
[phone ringing]

311
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:38,075
[phone ringing]

312
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:42,996
Emilia?

313
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:44,915
Hello, Raul. Where are you?

314
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:46,959
Uh… On my way home.

315
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:50,087
[scoffs] Whatever, Raul.
Just come home, okay?

316
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:54,007
[tense music playing]

317
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,051
[phone ringing]

318
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:01,849
[phone continues ringing]

319
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:03,350
[line ringing]

320
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,018
[pants] Emilia?

321
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:06,520
Hi! Hi, Jaguar.

322
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:08,230
I--I missed you. How are you?

323
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:09,606
[groans]

324
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,859
Huh? Hello? What's wrong?

325
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,820
-Nothing's wrong, Emilia.
-<i>Um…</i>

326
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:17,865
I'll get back to you
again later, okay? Bye.

327
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:20,701
[tense music playing]

328
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:25,122
[panting]

329
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:28,750
<i>Damn you, Damian.</i>

330
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:35,883
[gunfire]

331
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:40,012
[pants]

332
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:43,891
[gunfire continues]

333
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:45,767
Kill them.

334
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:48,312
[gunshots]

335
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:51,398
There are enemies at the back! Retreat!

336
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:53,358
We're surrounded! We need to go!

337
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:54,610
Come on!

338
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:57,112
[gunfire continues]

339
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:58,197
They're retreating.

340
00:19:58,614 --> 00:20:00,741
-Follow them! Hurry!
-[man 1] Come on!

341
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,618
Marlon, make sure
they don't come back here!

342
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:04,703
-[Marlon] I'm on it!
-You guys go with Marlon!

343
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,038
[Marlon] Come on! Come on!

344
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:07,122
[Jepoy] Ivy!

345
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,041
Ivy!

346
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,876
Hang on, Ivy!

347
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:12,085
[grunts]

348
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:15,631
-[men grunting]
-[shovels digging]

349
00:20:16,965 --> 00:20:18,050
[Ivy] <i>Mom…</i>

350
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:22,846
Mom…

351
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:25,933
Mom…

352
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:30,604
[instrumental theme music playing]

353
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:42,366
[somber music playing]

354
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,501
[Camia] <i>Please watch over my daughter.</i>

355
00:20:54,002 --> 00:20:56,922
<i>She still has to bring</i>
<i>those criminals to justice.</i>

356
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:00,050
<i>I'm begging you.</i>

357
00:21:02,719 --> 00:21:04,554
[men grunting]

358
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:10,686
[somber music continues playing]

359
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:26,493
[glass breaks]

360
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:34,960
Lily?

361
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,632
Ivy, we're coming!

362
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:45,887
[Diego groans]

363
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:50,475
[somber music continues playing]

364
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:54,021
[phone ringing]

365
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:02,070
[phone continues ringing]

366
00:22:06,283 --> 00:22:07,743
[Emilia] Hello!

367
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,662
Are you still breathing?

368
00:22:16,501 --> 00:22:21,798
Oh! According to my timer,
you've got one minute to live.

369
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:24,843
<i>Oh, Ivy.</i>

370
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:27,929
I do applaud your fighting spirit.

371
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:30,974
But you know? You always have
to remember that in life…

372
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:34,019
there's always a winner and a loser.

373
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:38,023
<i>It just so happened now that</i>
<i>you are the loser, and your end</i>

374
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:39,149
has come.

375
00:22:39,649 --> 00:22:41,068
Goodbye, my dear.

376
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:42,819
[ticking sound]

377
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:46,281
[Emilia] <i>So long, Ivy. </i>Adios!

378
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:47,991
[moans]

379
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:52,079
Cheers to your life.

380
00:22:52,746 --> 00:22:56,166
[laughing maniacally]

381
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,128
[Emilia continues laughing]

382
00:23:00,212 --> 00:23:02,255
[screaming]

383
00:23:04,382 --> 00:23:08,261
[Emilia laughing] <i>This is so nice!</i>

384
00:23:09,387 --> 00:23:12,641
[laughs] Victory for me!

385
00:23:12,724 --> 00:23:15,102
[laughing]

386
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:18,396
[raggedly breathing]

387
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:23,443
[dramatic music playing]

388
00:23:41,336 --> 00:23:44,089
[tense music playing]

389
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:05,235
-[Anna] Diego, Jepoy!
-Anna!

390
00:24:05,694 --> 00:24:07,988
Auntie Camia, they're back!

391
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:10,198
[both panting]

392
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:12,993
-Diego!
-Auntie.

393
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:15,620
Jepoy, where's my daughter?

394
00:24:18,832 --> 00:24:20,208
Where's Lily?

395
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:26,214
[dramatic music playing]

396
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:31,636
[Camia breathing heavily]

397
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:41,438
[panting]

398
00:24:44,941 --> 00:24:47,777
[Emilia] Lovely, I want my slit
a little higher.

399
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:50,739
And then, for the waist,
I want it like a corset.

400
00:24:50,822 --> 00:24:51,823
Make it tight.

401
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,992
Because I'm on a strict diet, you know?

402
00:24:54,075 --> 00:24:56,870
I want my waist accentuated, okay?

403
00:24:57,913 --> 00:25:01,458
-And regarding Papa's barong…
-This is what he'll wear.

404
00:25:02,292 --> 00:25:03,752
Hmm. Oh, well.

405
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:05,670
I'm positive he'll be
wearing a barong, okay?

406
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:07,005
-[Lovely] Okay.
-The food…

407
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:08,423
I'll discuss it tomorrow.

408
00:25:09,216 --> 00:25:12,219
-Hi, Papa.
-Hi there, Emilia.

409
00:25:12,302 --> 00:25:15,263
You seem to be in a good mood.

410
00:25:15,889 --> 00:25:19,893
Oh! I am, Papa, in a very good, good mood.

411
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:23,021
Because our dark days are over, Papa.

412
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,607
How come?

413
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:29,277
Because our enemy, Ivy Aguas, is dead.

414
00:25:29,361 --> 00:25:33,240
Isn't that supposed to be
a call for celebration?

415
00:25:33,323 --> 00:25:36,034
Ivy Aguas is dead.

416
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:38,453
Are you sure?

417
00:25:38,536 --> 00:25:40,747
I'm very, very sure, Papa.

418
00:25:40,830 --> 00:25:44,042
I was there, listening to
her last breath, Papa.

419
00:25:44,125 --> 00:25:46,044
In fact, my henchmen told me

420
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:49,631
that Diego Torillo tried to dig her out.

421
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:50,757
But they failed,

422
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:54,886
so I'm positive that Ivy Aguas is dead.

423
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:57,055
So, we should celebrate!

424
00:25:57,764 --> 00:26:01,685
Yeah, seems like it's a good
reason for celebration.

425
00:26:01,768 --> 00:26:02,852
Mm-hmm.

426
00:26:02,936 --> 00:26:04,437
Good job, Emilia.

427
00:26:04,854 --> 00:26:06,147
Thank you, Papa.

428
00:26:06,773 --> 00:26:07,774
[Julio] You know…

429
00:26:08,358 --> 00:26:10,944
we are going to have

430
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:15,573
the most amazing
centennial celebration ever.

431
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:21,413
And this will be the start
of a new chapter

432
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:25,208
of our reign over this province.

433
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:29,504
This will also mark our new beginning…

434
00:26:30,755 --> 00:26:32,340
as father and daughter.

435
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:33,466
[chuckles]

436
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:35,385
Oh.

437
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:38,179
-Cheers, Emilia!
-Oh!

438
00:26:39,139 --> 00:26:40,724
Cheers, Papa.

439
00:26:40,807 --> 00:26:42,100
[Julio chuckles]

440
00:26:43,768 --> 00:26:45,812
Excuse me, Papa.
I'll just fix our program.

441
00:26:46,229 --> 00:26:47,397
Go ahead, go ahead.

442
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:48,982
[Emilia] Ladies…

443
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:51,609
Colonel!

444
00:26:52,068 --> 00:26:55,530
Do you have any more good news to share?

445
00:26:55,613 --> 00:26:58,283
Well, sir, I finally know
who's been supporting

446
00:26:58,366 --> 00:27:00,618
Diego Torillo and encouraging
him to go against us.

447
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:04,956
-Who?
-Vice Governor Mateo Ruiz.

448
00:27:05,665 --> 00:27:07,208
[chuckling]

449
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:12,797
These so-called goody two-shoes sure know

450
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:14,966
how to stab you in the back.

451
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:18,720
Anyway, I will deal

452
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:22,807
with that two-faced miscreant
of a vice governor.

453
00:27:23,433 --> 00:27:24,809
Just wait and see.

454
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:28,938
[tense music playing]

455
00:27:39,282 --> 00:27:41,409
[secretary]
This is for you, Vice Governor.

456
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:43,036
You may leave.

457
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:51,920
[tense music playing]

458
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:05,558
Governor! What a surprise!

459
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:09,562
Well, not as surprised as I am, Vice.

460
00:28:09,979 --> 00:28:11,773
So, what are we discussing today?

461
00:28:11,856 --> 00:28:13,066
[chuckles]

462
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:16,444
Let's cut to the chase.

463
00:28:20,698 --> 00:28:22,951
You have been sleeping with the enemy.

464
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:27,789
Your enemy, Governor, not mine.

465
00:28:29,958 --> 00:28:32,544
And here I thought you were different.

466
00:28:33,002 --> 00:28:36,172
That despite our differences
in parties and principles,

467
00:28:36,256 --> 00:28:39,759
you wouldn't dare snatch the position

468
00:28:40,093 --> 00:28:43,012
I won fair and square.

469
00:28:43,972 --> 00:28:45,140
But, no.

470
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:46,975
Now I find out…

471
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:52,147
that you'll even use
that amateur, Diego Torillo.

472
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:55,859
Now, that is a shocker.

473
00:28:55,942 --> 00:28:57,360
It's a low blow…

474
00:28:58,236 --> 00:29:02,949
considering you don't even
strike me as the ambitious kind.

475
00:29:04,534 --> 00:29:05,994
That's true, Governor.

476
00:29:06,494 --> 00:29:08,455
I'm not the ambitious type.

477
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:10,999
But I do have integrity.

478
00:29:12,292 --> 00:29:14,252
Diego Torillo was the one
who approached me,

479
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:17,005
and I think it's for a good cause.

480
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:20,508
Oh, let's cut the political talk.

481
00:29:21,092 --> 00:29:22,385
Let's just be real.

482
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:27,140
I'm helping Diego not because
I want to bring you down,

483
00:29:27,474 --> 00:29:30,643
but because I believe in what's right.

484
00:29:31,603 --> 00:29:34,606
Now, if the election really was rigged…

485
00:29:36,566 --> 00:29:38,485
it's only right that you pay for it.

486
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:44,991
There's been news going around

487
00:29:45,074 --> 00:29:47,660
that Julio's planning to move
his office to the capitol.

488
00:29:48,328 --> 00:29:51,039
I also heard they're busy preparing

489
00:29:51,122 --> 00:29:53,541
for the centennial celebration.

490
00:29:54,167 --> 00:29:57,253
They say it'll be their victory party.

491
00:29:57,712 --> 00:29:59,172
Those bastards!

492
00:29:59,839 --> 00:30:01,257
If Lily were here,

493
00:30:01,341 --> 00:30:03,510
there's no way she'd let Julio Ardiente

494
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:07,138
get away with rigging the entire election!

495
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:08,973
Then for her sake…

496
00:30:10,016 --> 00:30:11,559
we won't give up.

497
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:16,231
We'll keep fighting and remove
Julio Ardiente from power.

498
00:30:16,481 --> 00:30:21,277
We can't let my daughter's
sacrifices be for nothing.

499
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:24,364
[tense music playing]

500
00:30:31,955 --> 00:30:37,085
Funny for you to be waving
the flag of justice,

501
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:41,339
when I know for certain that
at one time or another,

502
00:30:41,422 --> 00:30:43,550
you did things you weren't proud of.

503
00:30:44,050 --> 00:30:49,180
It being that you are an ex-military man.

504
00:30:50,014 --> 00:30:54,060
Investigate me all you want.
You won't find anything.

505
00:30:54,602 --> 00:30:57,021
I'm a straight-laced politician, Governor.

506
00:30:57,564 --> 00:30:59,524
I've got news for you, Vice.

507
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:04,529
All politicians have their
fair share of dirty laundry.

508
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:10,243
It's just a matter of finding
the skeletons in your closet.

509
00:31:10,785 --> 00:31:13,830
And believe me, I will find them.

510
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:17,000
If you don't stop this nonsense.

511
00:31:17,667 --> 00:31:19,377
If I were you, Governor…

512
00:31:19,961 --> 00:31:23,214
I'd postpone this celebration of yours.

513
00:31:24,048 --> 00:31:25,967
You don't scare me.

514
00:31:27,051 --> 00:31:29,220
[clicks tongue] Well then.

515
00:31:31,222 --> 00:31:33,016
We'll just have to see about that.

516
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:41,065
Don't get on my bad side, Vice.

517
00:31:41,941 --> 00:31:43,776
You won't like what you find.

518
00:31:45,153 --> 00:31:48,823
[tense music playing]

519
00:31:50,325 --> 00:31:51,326
[sighs]

520
00:31:59,667 --> 00:32:02,211
[tense music continues]

521
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:08,760
I still can't believe it, Diego.

522
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:12,805
How could they do such a thing to Lily?

523
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:17,268
[sentimental music playing]

524
00:32:17,352 --> 00:32:18,519
Don't give up, Anna.

525
00:32:20,396 --> 00:32:22,857
Ivy would say the same thing
if she were here.

526
00:32:25,026 --> 00:32:28,363
You know how she is.
She can take care of herself.

527
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:30,740
She'll keep fighting and never give up.

528
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:36,120
And that's why we can't, either.

529
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:45,254
Okay, I'll just go talk to the others.

530
00:32:45,463 --> 00:32:48,299
[sentimental music continues]

531
00:32:55,890 --> 00:32:56,933
Diego.

532
00:32:58,726 --> 00:32:59,894
Tell it to me straight.

533
00:33:02,146 --> 00:33:03,773
How do you feel about my friend, Anna?

534
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:08,736
-What are you--
-You know what I mean, Diego.

535
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:10,863
You're a guy. You know she likes you.

536
00:33:11,364 --> 00:33:13,116
-Jepoy--
-Are you making moves on her

537
00:33:13,199 --> 00:33:14,409
now that Ivy's gone?

538
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:17,620
Jepoy, I respect you as Ivy's friend.

539
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:21,207
So don't take my friendship
with Anna the wrong way.

540
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:23,793
There's only one woman I love.

541
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,963
And that's never going to change.

542
00:33:28,506 --> 00:33:29,632
Remember that.

543
00:33:29,966 --> 00:33:33,052
[tense music playing]

544
00:33:47,066 --> 00:33:48,151
Oh, Raul.

545
00:33:48,401 --> 00:33:50,945
Where were you, and what is that?

546
00:33:51,738 --> 00:33:53,656
-It's nothing.
-Nothing?

547
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:56,075
It's too early for another fight, Emilia.

548
00:33:56,325 --> 00:33:57,869
Excuse me, Raul.

549
00:33:57,952 --> 00:33:59,370
Didn't I call you last night

550
00:33:59,454 --> 00:34:02,415
because I was worried,
and this is how you treat me?

551
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,083
Wait.

552
00:34:04,333 --> 00:34:06,627
Did you really call
because you were worried,

553
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:10,089
or is it because it's your
obligation as my wife?

554
00:34:10,465 --> 00:34:13,009
And why are you always
so on edge when we talk,

555
00:34:13,092 --> 00:34:14,510
but with other men, you're oh-so-sweet?

556
00:34:14,594 --> 00:34:17,513
[scoffs] Have you been listening
to my calls?

557
00:34:17,597 --> 00:34:19,724
No, why? Is it true
what they say about you?

558
00:34:19,807 --> 00:34:20,892
Are you guilty?

559
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:24,270
Wow! Me? I think it's you who's guilty.

560
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:26,355
-You can't fool me, Raul.
-[scoffs]

561
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:30,526
You think I don't know that
you're working with Diego

562
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:31,694
and Ivy Aguas?

563
00:34:32,111 --> 00:34:33,780
I already know, Raul, okay?

564
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:34,781
But I don't care.

565
00:34:34,864 --> 00:34:38,451
It doesn't matter right now
because Ivy Aguas is dead, okay?

566
00:34:39,869 --> 00:34:40,787
Oops.

567
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:44,582
Wait. Tell that to your son.

568
00:34:44,999 --> 00:34:46,751
Ivy Aguas is dead.

569
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:54,926
[tense music playing]

570
00:35:04,769 --> 00:35:06,729
All right, I'll see you both
at the capitol.

571
00:35:06,813 --> 00:35:07,730
-Okay.
-Sure.

572
00:35:07,814 --> 00:35:09,023
-Take care.
-We have to be there.

573
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:09,941
Take care.

574
00:35:10,608 --> 00:35:11,692
[Damian] Camia.

575
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:15,822
Damian, where were you?

576
00:35:21,661 --> 00:35:23,162
How's Ivy doing?

577
00:35:25,915 --> 00:35:28,417
They buried my daughter alive.

578
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:32,130
How do you think she's doing?

579
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:36,008
I'm tired of crying and getting hurt.

580
00:35:37,885 --> 00:35:39,804
The Ardientes need to pay

581
00:35:39,887 --> 00:35:42,723
for what they did to my daughter
and this province.

582
00:35:43,099 --> 00:35:45,726
[tense music playing]

583
00:35:49,313 --> 00:35:52,942
[protesters chanting]
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

584
00:35:53,025 --> 00:35:56,279
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

585
00:35:56,362 --> 00:36:00,199
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

586
00:36:00,283 --> 00:36:03,578
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

587
00:36:03,661 --> 00:36:06,956
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

588
00:36:07,039 --> 00:36:10,668
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

589
00:36:10,751 --> 00:36:14,130
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

590
00:36:14,213 --> 00:36:17,800
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

591
00:36:17,884 --> 00:36:19,510
Julio Ardiente…

592
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:24,974
Earlier today, Julio Ardiente
threatened Vice Governor Ruiz,

593
00:36:25,057 --> 00:36:28,477
saying that he shouldn't support
my complaint against him.

594
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:35,484
We are sick and tired of all these threats

595
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:37,862
just to cover up the truth.

596
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:43,117
Julio Ardiente has to be ousted!

597
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:48,372
And pay for what he did
to this province, to Diego,

598
00:36:48,456 --> 00:36:51,792
and to everyone who opposes him!

599
00:36:52,126 --> 00:36:53,085
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

600
00:36:53,169 --> 00:36:55,046
-That's right!
-Impeach him!

601
00:36:55,796 --> 00:36:59,133
[protesters chanting]
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

602
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:02,887
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

603
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:06,265
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

604
00:37:06,349 --> 00:37:09,810
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

605
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:13,314
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

606
00:37:13,397 --> 00:37:16,692
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

607
00:37:16,776 --> 00:37:20,363
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

608
00:37:20,446 --> 00:37:23,699
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

609
00:37:23,783 --> 00:37:27,036
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

610
00:37:27,119 --> 00:37:30,581
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

611
00:37:30,665 --> 00:37:35,503
Julio Ardiente is a cheater! Cheater!

612
00:37:35,586 --> 00:37:36,879
Are you done yet?

613
00:37:36,963 --> 00:37:40,258
[tense music playing]

614
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:43,844
You're like a broken record,
a pain to the ears.

615
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:47,556
But that's your right. Now, it's my turn.

616
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:49,892
First of all,

617
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:56,524
I would like to wholeheartedly
thank the citizens of Ardiente

618
00:37:56,607 --> 00:38:01,821
who showed their love and support

619
00:38:02,363 --> 00:38:07,159
so that your true leader
could assume office.

620
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:13,874
Now, for all my opponents,
the rivals that I've defeated,

621
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:16,294
those sore losers

622
00:38:18,045 --> 00:38:23,801
who've done nothing
but find fault in my victory,

623
00:38:24,677 --> 00:38:29,348
all I can say is, please be a good sport.

624
00:38:29,932 --> 00:38:32,852
Truth is, you don't have anything on me.

625
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:38,399
You can keep complaining, but
the Ardientes will always win.

626
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:41,569
Because anyone who opposes you

627
00:38:41,652 --> 00:38:45,906
ends up either dead
or buried in the ground!

628
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:48,159
Just like what you did to Ivy Aguas!

629
00:38:48,242 --> 00:38:49,827
-Huh?
-[protesters] Yeah!

630
00:38:49,910 --> 00:38:51,537
-That's right!
-He's right!

631
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:52,830
-Murderer!
-[Julio] Ivy Aguas?

632
00:38:53,289 --> 00:38:56,000
Ivy Aguas was an ally.

633
00:38:56,667 --> 00:38:59,837
She's been a big help to this election.

634
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:01,464
Why would I have her killed?

635
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,215
And don't forget, Diego…

636
00:39:03,716 --> 00:39:08,596
Didn't I offer to lend you some of my men

637
00:39:09,638 --> 00:39:12,558
to look for Ivy Aguas?

638
00:39:12,975 --> 00:39:14,226
You liar!

639
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:15,561
[Julio] Huh? Oh, dear.

640
00:39:15,644 --> 00:39:18,147
Camia, we didn't do anything wrong.

641
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:20,733
That's the truth. Just accept it.

642
00:39:20,816 --> 00:39:22,485
Ivy's dead, and that's it.

643
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:30,826
So, to the loved ones of Ivy Aguas,

644
00:39:30,910 --> 00:39:32,119
our thoughts are with you.

645
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:38,417
This is all I have to say…

646
00:39:38,876 --> 00:39:41,045
It pains me to say this,

647
00:39:41,796 --> 00:39:42,755
but the truth is,

648
00:39:44,090 --> 00:39:47,176
Ivy Aguas played with fire.

649
00:39:47,968 --> 00:39:53,307
And when you play with fire,
you usually get burned.

650
00:39:54,517 --> 00:39:56,644
This is just a reminder to everyone,

651
00:39:57,561 --> 00:40:00,064
so you won't end up like her.

652
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:03,317
You are a family of murderers!

653
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:07,696
[tense music playing]

654
00:40:23,671 --> 00:40:26,757
[tense music playing]

655
00:40:36,016 --> 00:40:37,017
Boss.

656
00:40:38,185 --> 00:40:39,437
What are you doing here?

657
00:40:41,021 --> 00:40:43,816
The men in our hideout
were talking about you.

658
00:40:44,733 --> 00:40:47,653
They're wondering
if you're neglecting our operations.

659
00:40:49,488 --> 00:40:52,491
Not now, Fabian. Leave me be.

660
00:40:53,492 --> 00:40:55,661
Looks like your priorities
have changed, boss.

661
00:40:57,204 --> 00:40:59,748
I hope you don't wait
for ours to change too.

662
00:41:00,291 --> 00:41:03,627
[tense music playing]

663
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:12,428
Diego, Diego…

664
00:41:13,512 --> 00:41:15,222
You never learn, do you?

665
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:18,309
After all those years
you lived in my house,

666
00:41:18,767 --> 00:41:21,604
believing you were an Ardiente,

667
00:41:22,062 --> 00:41:24,523
after all those years from your childhood,

668
00:41:25,733 --> 00:41:29,653
you never learned anything
from me regarding politics.

669
00:41:30,696 --> 00:41:31,906
Look at you now.

670
00:41:32,823 --> 00:41:37,995
You're nothing but a pathetic sore loser.

671
00:41:40,664 --> 00:41:41,957
You're the loser here.

672
00:41:42,666 --> 00:41:45,961
You cheated in the election
because you were losing to me.

673
00:41:46,045 --> 00:41:47,171
You couldn't accept the fact

674
00:41:47,254 --> 00:41:49,965
that you were losing to a bastard like me!

675
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:52,301
[chuckling]

676
00:41:54,345 --> 00:42:00,267
Diego, you're throwing pebbles
at a mighty wall.

677
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:02,978
But anyway, go ahead.

678
00:42:03,604 --> 00:42:06,232
Keep accusing me.

679
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:09,777
Sue me if you want.
Do whatever you please.

680
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:11,946
But at the end of the day,

681
00:42:12,029 --> 00:42:16,992
I will still be standing
as governor of Ardiente.

682
00:42:18,744 --> 00:42:19,787
[camera shutter clicks]

683
00:42:19,870 --> 00:42:25,209
[Julio] And if,
by some stroke of a miracle,

684
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:29,046
you manage to kick me out of my position,

685
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:31,632
just as you've been meaning to do,

686
00:42:33,425 --> 00:42:36,470
haven't you realized that you
won't gain anything from it?

687
00:42:39,181 --> 00:42:47,064
Because some Pontius Pilate will just
take advantage of all your hard work.

688
00:42:47,147 --> 00:42:48,148
Don't you agree?

689
00:42:49,024 --> 00:42:50,317
That's what you think.

690
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:55,197
Enjoy yourself while you still can.

691
00:42:56,699 --> 00:42:58,534
Because mark my words…

692
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:01,704
I will make sure
to bring your family down.

693
00:43:01,787 --> 00:43:03,914
My, my, Diego…

694
00:43:05,207 --> 00:43:06,792
What's this? Are you hearing yourself?

695
00:43:08,043 --> 00:43:09,962
What I see is rage.

696
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:14,341
Undirected, misguided rage.

697
00:43:14,425 --> 00:43:18,804
Anyway, like I said, do whatever you want.

698
00:43:19,221 --> 00:43:21,682
I will welcome all your accusations.

699
00:43:21,974 --> 00:43:23,517
But in the end…

700
00:43:24,852 --> 00:43:27,354
Julio Ardiente will still be the governor.

701
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:28,981
You're wrong.

702
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,943
Like I said, enjoy while you still can.

703
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:36,363
Because I will make sure…

704
00:43:36,947 --> 00:43:39,658
I will make sure of
your family's downfall.

705
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:44,997
Well, good luck in
your endeavors, Diego Torillo.

706
00:43:46,373 --> 00:43:48,751
But I'm telling you,

707
00:43:49,543 --> 00:43:52,588
all your efforts will be in vain.

708
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:55,633
It's like riding a stationary bike.

709
00:43:56,091 --> 00:44:00,512
You keep pedaling,
but you're going nowhere.

710
00:44:01,889 --> 00:44:03,724
But I applaud you people.

711
00:44:03,807 --> 00:44:08,312
Please, please continue
upholding your cause,

712
00:44:08,395 --> 00:44:12,232
for what you believe in.
I will not stop you.

713
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:16,403
You have all the right
to voice out your opinions.

714
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:21,992
This is also to prove
that we Ardientes fight fair

715
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:25,371
and that we believe in democracy.

716
00:44:26,538 --> 00:44:27,539
For now…

717
00:44:28,916 --> 00:44:32,378
Please excuse me. <i>Adios!</i>

718
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:34,838
-[man] You cheated!
-[Loring] Cheater!

719
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:38,175
[protesters chanting]
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

720
00:44:38,258 --> 00:44:42,304
-[laughing maniacally]
-Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

721
00:44:42,388 --> 00:44:45,808
-[Loring] Cheater!
-Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

722
00:44:45,891 --> 00:44:49,311
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

723
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:52,731
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

724
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:56,902
<i>We report the passing</i>
<i>of renowned businesswoman</i>

725
00:44:56,985 --> 00:45:01,323
<i>and a staunch supporter of</i>
<i>the Ardientes, Ivy Aguas.</i>

726
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:03,700
<i>This was confirmed by her</i>
<i>friend, Emilia Ardiente-Torillo,</i>

727
00:45:03,784 --> 00:45:08,205
<i>who, at one point, almost</i>
<i>became her mother-in-law.</i>

728
00:45:08,288 --> 00:45:11,417
Any statement on Ivy Aguas'
passing, ma'am?

729
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:12,709
<i>I had nothing to do with it.</i>

730
00:45:12,793 --> 00:45:15,421
<i>I think I've answered</i>
<i>that question many times,</i>

731
00:45:15,504 --> 00:45:17,506
<i>and I would still have the same answer.</i>

732
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:19,508
<i>I had nothing to do with it. Thank you.</i>

733
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:22,928
[reporter] <i>Stay tuned for more details.</i>

734
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:26,807
[tense music playing]

735
00:45:40,779 --> 00:45:41,864
Emilia.

736
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:47,411
Did you have Ivy Aguas killed?

737
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:51,165
And what makes you think that?

738
00:45:51,331 --> 00:45:52,958
Oh, come on, Emilia.

739
00:45:53,459 --> 00:45:56,211
I know my wife inside out.

740
00:45:56,545 --> 00:45:59,506
You're a master when it comes
to dispatching people.

741
00:46:01,383 --> 00:46:05,721
You know, Raul,
the reason why I'm still free

742
00:46:05,804 --> 00:46:08,807
is that those people
have no evidence against me.

743
00:46:09,308 --> 00:46:13,937
And that will also be the case
regarding Ivy Aguas' death.

744
00:46:14,897 --> 00:46:17,649
[tense music playing]

745
00:46:22,696 --> 00:46:24,364
Ivy may be gone now,

746
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:28,744
but I will never forget how she
helped us against the Ardientes,

747
00:46:28,827 --> 00:46:31,497
especially when we were
almost killed by the governor.

748
00:46:31,580 --> 00:46:34,208
I admire her even more now.

749
00:46:36,084 --> 00:46:41,256
We shall see to it that her
efforts won't ever be in vain…

750
00:46:42,341 --> 00:46:46,011
that they will continue
to haunt the Ardiente family.

751
00:46:46,094 --> 00:46:49,556
[pensive music playing]

752
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:03,654
Sir?

753
00:47:05,030 --> 00:47:06,365
What brings you here?

754
00:47:07,950 --> 00:47:09,451
I have good news, Diego.

755
00:47:11,036 --> 00:47:14,206
Election Commission Secretary
Martel has finally agreed

756
00:47:14,289 --> 00:47:16,083
to hear out our complaints.

757
00:47:17,084 --> 00:47:18,835
Thank you very much, sir.

758
00:47:20,128 --> 00:47:21,630
Thank you too.

759
00:47:22,130 --> 00:47:24,883
The media and Malacañang
noticed the noise you generated.

760
00:47:24,967 --> 00:47:27,719
That's why we were given an audience
with the Election Commission.

761
00:47:31,640 --> 00:47:34,017
We're going up against
a powerful man, Diego.

762
00:47:35,686 --> 00:47:37,980
Are you sure about this?

763
00:47:38,063 --> 00:47:39,565
I won't back out.

764
00:47:40,148 --> 00:47:41,149
Everything's ready.

765
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:43,694
We're taking down Julio Ardiente.

766
00:47:50,951 --> 00:47:53,495
[breathes deeply]

767
00:47:56,665 --> 00:48:00,669
[sinister music playing]

768
00:48:03,964 --> 00:48:04,881
No.

769
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:08,051
Come on, Emilia. [nervous chuckle]

770
00:48:08,135 --> 00:48:10,220
This is not happening. Come on.

771
00:48:10,679 --> 00:48:14,224
You're watching too many horror movies.

772
00:48:14,808 --> 00:48:16,059
This is not happening.

773
00:48:16,143 --> 00:48:19,646
[ominous music playing]

774
00:48:27,904 --> 00:48:30,699
[suspenseful music plays]

775
00:48:30,782 --> 00:48:31,825
[shudders]

776
00:48:34,494 --> 00:48:39,958
[Ivy] <i>Mark my words, Emilia.</i>
<i>If I die, I will haunt you.</i>

777
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:42,836
[shrieking]

778
00:48:42,919 --> 00:48:45,672
Papa! Raul!

779
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:47,215
[shrieks]

780
00:48:47,841 --> 00:48:51,345
[suspenseful music playing]

781
00:48:54,848 --> 00:48:56,725
<i>Do you know what you're</i>
<i>getting yourself into?</i>

782
00:48:56,808 --> 00:48:59,061
<i>I'm not scared</i>
<i>because I know someone powerful,</i>

783
00:48:59,144 --> 00:49:02,606
<i>more powerful than that</i>
<i>politician you're protecting!</i>

784
00:49:02,689 --> 00:49:07,194
[Julio] <i>Who else dared to go against me?</i>

785
00:49:07,277 --> 00:49:08,612
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

786
00:49:08,695 --> 00:49:11,531
<i>I want you to hunt down Lily Cruz.</i>

787
00:49:11,615 --> 00:49:13,283
<i>I want her dead!</i>

788
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:14,451
[Jepoy] <i>This is getting too risky, Anna.</i>

789
00:49:14,534 --> 00:49:16,536
<i>If your life was in danger</i>
<i>before, it's worse now.</i>

790
00:49:16,620 --> 00:49:18,872
<i>Dead people belong in the grave.</i>

791
00:49:18,955 --> 00:49:22,584
<i>Who's this from?!</i>
<i>Get that thing away from me!</i>

792
00:49:22,834 --> 00:49:25,087
[Jose] <i>What are you going</i>
<i>to do now? Jump off this cliff?</i>

793
00:49:25,420 --> 00:49:26,505
<i>Or get shot?</i>

794
00:49:27,756 --> 00:49:30,300
[theme music playing]
